# oracle: fix adapt on pair coul/streitz 12.0 wolf 0.3 alpha (g_wolf scaled down every 5 steps, reset no): the force loop reads alpha as it is then, the Wolf self terms woself and dwoself keep the pair_coeff one; then a second run from the new alpha
# oracle-potentials: AlO.streitz
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
units           metal
atom_style      charge
boundary        p p p
lattice         none 1.0
region          box block 0 10 0 10 0 10
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 random 16 12345 box
create_atoms    2 random 16 54321 box
mass            1 26.981539
mass            2 15.9994
set             type 1 charge 1.2
set             type 2 charge -0.8
variable        vx atom 0.02*sin(id)
variable        vy atom 0.02*cos(2*id)
variable        vz atom 0.02*sin(3*id)
pair_style      coul/streitz 12.0 wolf 0.3
pair_coeff      * * AlO.streitz Al O
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz
timestep        0.0002
fix             1 all nve
variable        s equal 1.0-0.01*elapsed
fix             2 all adapt 5 pair coul/streitz alpha * * v_s scale yes reset no
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong ke press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          5
run             30
run             20
